From a6baba6a9d4b8b0a8e9facd3b6d6dc1dae87b3f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tts-engine-overhaul <dev@local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:03:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Route TTS through established OS speech engines; honor engine
 selection

Why: OS-level TTS was effectively faked. 'OS Neural Voices' and 'OS
Classic Voices' previews spoke through the Web Speech API, but every
FILE RENDER (TTS Studio, AutoBook, Audiobook Studio) silently re-
rendered with the built-in formant engine. Engine selection was also
inert: system-neural vs system-classic never reached the voice picker,
so pickBestVoice always chose neural voices regardless of the model.

Established OS engines (new local bridge, zero deps):
- scripts/os-tts-server.mjs: localhost companion server that renders
  WAV through Windows SAPI 5 (System.Speech), macOS Apple Speech (say),
  Linux espeak-ng/espeak, and optional Piper neural voices. Loopback
  only, temp-dir renders, request caps, hung-process timeouts.
- src/lib/engines/os-tts-bridge.ts: client probe/voice-list/synthesize,
  manual RIFF/WAVE parser (PCM 8/16/24/32 + float32) -> AudioBuffer,
  per-engine capability table, configurable bridge URL (localStorage).
- npm run os-tts starts it; TTS Studio shows live bridge status.

Engine selection is now real:
- src/lib/engines/dispatch.ts: single dispatcher routes synthesis to
  the SELECTED model's engine (os-bridge -> real OS engine; system-* ->
  OS bridge when running, else explicit formant fallback with reason).
  Markup-aware OS render planning ([pause]/[rate]/[pitch]/[whisper]),
  sentence-aligned chunking with breathing gaps, volume compensation
  for engines without a volume control.
- speech.ts: voiceClass-aware scoring (scoreVoiceForClass) so classic
  models pick classic local voices and neural models pick neural ones;
  pickVoiceForOptions resolves explicit voiceURI first.
- Every render logs 'Engine actually used: <engine>'.

Views:
- tts-studio: previews via the real OS engine for bridge models,
  voiceClass passed for system models; OS bridge status strip with
  retry + custom URL; dynamic (honest) engine notes; render meta now
  records the engine that actually produced the file.
- autobook: production narration dispatches through the selected
  engine; cast profiles map deterministically to distinct OS voices
  (gender-matched, stable cycling) so characters stay distinguishable.
- audiobook: chapter renders dispatch through the selected engine.

Realism improvements:
- formant engine: wh-question falling contours (only yes/no questions
  rise), occasional longer narrator breaths between long sentences,
  softer sibilance; system voice ranking gains class-aware scoring.
- tts-models catalog: new 'OS Speech Engine (native)' (now the default
  selection) and 'Piper Neural (OS Bridge)' models with honest
  descriptions of what each engine renders.

Tests: tests/os-bridge-smoke.mts (WAV parser vs real espeak-ng render,
voice-class ranking, profile->OS-voice mapping, catalog defaults);
alias loader resolves extensionless relative imports.

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean, eslint clean, next build succeeds,
engine suite 44/44, bridge smoke 15/15, live espeak-ng render through
the bridge (22050 Hz 16-bit WAV) decoded by the client parser.
